<title>FRANCE: Alcatel wins 280 mln franc Swiss army contract.</title>
<headline>Alcatel wins 280 mln franc Swiss army contract.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alcatel Telecom, a unit of Alcatel Alsthom, said it had signed a 280 million French franc contract with the Swiss army for the delivery of 450 digital tranmission stations for a Herzian radio wave network.</p>
<p>The stations will use the High bitrate Digital Subscriber Line (HDSL) technology and will become part of Switzerland's Integrated Military Telecommunications System.</p>
</text>
